# Expectation record for 03_initializers/005_designated_struct.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 005_designated_struct
area               = 03_initializers
description        = Designated struct member initializers: declaration order and reversed order, omitted members, a designator reaching through a member into a submember, a positional value resuming after a member designator, and designators descending into an element of an array member -- seven forms at static duration and four again at automatic duration, every member read back individually
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined and no unspecified behaviour, which is the precondition that
makes both differential oracles sound: undefined behaviour would license either compiler to do
anything at all, so a divergence over it would prove nothing about either one.
No uninitialized storage is ever read, which is the first thing to check in a program that prints
members its initializers never mention. A member or element left unmentioned by a brace-enclosed
initializer is initialized as an object of static storage duration would be -- that is, to zero --
for automatic and static duration alike (C11 6.7.9p19 and p21), so every member printed here has a
determinate value and the zero lines are assertions rather than accidents. That applies to
g_omitted's whole nested member, to g_nested_mem's sibling submember and trailing scalar, to
g_then_pos's tag, to the three untouched elements of g_arr_elem.a, and to the automatic-duration
twins l_omitted and l_arr_elem exactly as it does to the statics, because an object with any
initializer is fully initialized.
Every designator names a member that exists in the type it designates, and every array-element
designator names an index strictly inside that member's declared bounds. No designator in this
program designates the same subobject twice, so the last-designator-wins resolution is never relied
on. Every initializer expression is an integer constant expression with no side effects, so C11
6.7.9p23 -- which leaves the order of an initializer list's evaluations indeterminately sequenced
and therefore the order of their side effects unspecified -- has nothing to act on, and the
program's meaning does not depend on the order the list is processed in. Reordering designators
changes only which member each value reaches, not the order in which any side effect occurs,
because there are none.
No arithmetic is performed on any initialized value, so no signed overflow is possible; the only
arithmetic in the file is the loop counter's increment over the range 0 through 3. Nothing is
shifted, divided or remaindered. Nothing is modified after its initialization, so no object is
modified twice between two sequence points.
Every subscript is the loop counter strictly less than 4 indexing an int[4] array member, so no
out-of-bounds access occurs and no one-past-the-end pointer is formed. There is no pointer cast, no
pointer arithmetic and no pointer of any kind in the program apart from printf's format argument;
no address is taken and none is printed.
There is no aliasing violation: every object is read only through an lvalue of its own declared
type, which is int in every case, reached by member selection and subscripting. No object
representation is examined, no object is printed, copied or reinterpreted as bytes, and no cast
appears anywhere in the file, so no padding byte is observed and nothing depends on the relative
addresses of unrelated objects.
Every initializer value is a small positive int, the largest being 104, so each is representable in
int on every target the suite supports and no implicit conversion changes a value.
Every printf call receives arguments free of side effects -- a loop counter and one int member -- so
the unspecified order in which a function call's arguments are evaluated cannot affect the output.
%d is the only conversion specifier in the file and every corresponding argument has type int after
the default argument promotions, so no variadic argument is read at the wrong width.
main returns a constant 0, inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is
truncated by the operating system. Every input is a literal in this file: nothing is read from the
environment, the clock, the file system or the network, and iteration order is fixed by literal
bounds, so every cell is reproducible from this source and this record alone.
No header is included anywhere and printf is declared by hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);`.
bcc bundles the nine required freestanding headers plus a bonus stdatomic.h and ships no standard
I/O header (docs/project-guide.md line 212), so naming one would fail on the bcc side of oracle (a)
while succeeding on the reference side -- a spurious divergence caused by the test rather than by a
compiler. This area is granted no header exception; the corpus has exactly two, area 07's stdarg.h
and the dedicated bundled-header probe in area 12.
This record declares no warning-gate deviation, and area 03 sanctions none. The program is clean
under the full default gate -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow
-Werror at -O0, -O1 and -O2 with all four reference drivers, and it builds and runs clean under the
sanitizer gate -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all. Both gates are
reference-compiler-only and are never applied to bcc, so requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is
untouched.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This record narrows nothing: all four targets, all three optimization levels and all three
oracles are enabled, no expected-divergence marker is carried, and no implementation-defined
value reaches this program's output. No `ub_audit_flags` key appears because the program passes
the suite's full default warning gate unmodified.
WHY OMITTING MEMBERS IS GATE-CLEAN HERE AND THIS RECORD NEEDS NO DEVIATION. -Wextra enables
-Wmissing-field-initializers and -Werror promotes it, but in C that diagnostic does not fire for a
designated initializer, only for a positional partial one such as a lone leading value. Every
initializer in this program is designated, so leaving members unmentioned is both legal and quiet.
None of them may be rewritten in positional form: doing so would trade the construct under test
for a diagnostic. The positional partial spelling is covered separately, in
003_partial_zero_fill.c, where it carries the scoped pragma that spelling requires.
STATIC AND AUTOMATIC DURATION ARE THE TWO VARIANTS HERE, and no operand in this program is
volatile -- deliberately, rather than as an omission of the suite's two-variant discipline. An
initializer for an object of static storage duration is a constant expression evaluated at
translation time and materialized into a data or BSS image, so it exercises the path that computes
an initial image; the same initializer at automatic storage duration is performed by emitted
instructions on entry to the block, so it exercises the path that generates stores. The g_ objects
take the first path and the l_ objects the second. With optimization off the statics appear as
data-section bytes while the twins appear as a run of stores into the frame, and at a higher level
either path may be folded into immediate operands, which is what makes all three optimization
levels informative; a compiler can implement one correctly and the other incorrectly, so both are
compiled at all three levels and their answers are printed separately. A volatile aggregate would
change the accesses under test rather than force the initializer to be performed at run time, which
the storage duration already does, and the subject here is what an initializer produces rather than
what an operator computes.
WIDTH NORMALIZATION. Every member of every structure is an int and %d is the only conversion
specifier in the file, so nothing whose width varies by target is declared, computed or printed. No
long, size_t, ptrdiff_t, intptr_t, float or double appears, no length modifier is used, no sizeof or
_Alignof result is printed and no address is printed, so the MEASURED i686 difference -- a four-byte
long and pointer against eight bytes on x86-64, AArch64 and RISC-V 64
(docs/technical-specifications.md target table, lines 457-462) -- cannot surface, and no layout
choice the ABI is free to make is observable. Only the values the designators place, and the zeros
the standard guarantees between them, are.
PLAIN-CHAR SIGNEDNESS. No character data appears at all, so the MEASURED split -- signed on x86-64
and i686, unsigned on AArch64 and RISC-V 64 -- is irrelevant here.
PADDING. Members are read individually by name and no object is ever printed, copied or
reinterpreted as bytes, so padding, whose contents the standard leaves unspecified, is never
observed.
EXECUTION CHARACTER SET. Nothing character-valued is printed, so C11 5.2.1 leaves nothing here to
the implementation.
WHERE THE GOLDEN BYTES CARRY THE MOST INFORMATION. The sharpest case in the program is g_then_pos:
after the member designator .in the current object advances to the member FOLLOWING in, so the bare
44 lands in trailer while tag -- which precedes the designated member and is never mentioned --
stays at its implicit zero. A compiler that restarted at the first member, or that advanced by the
wrong number of members, produces a visibly different four-line group rather than a subtly wrong
single value. The struct that carries a nested struct member places it BETWEEN two scalars for the
same reason, so a layout or traversal error shifts a value that is printed rather than hiding in a
slot nobody reads.
MEASURED EVIDENCE. The program was compiled with the reference driver for all four targets at -O0,
-O1 and -O2 -- twelve configurations -- and every one produced these 50 lines byte-identically with
exit status 0, which is why oracle (b) compares this program's targets against each other without
any narrowing and why oracle (c) can hold these bytes as the golden record. The output is 50 fixed
key=value lines in a fixed order, one per member observed, so a single divergent line localizes to a
single member of a single initializer form rather than to the program as a whole.
END
